   escalation_note — v1.0

   The internal handover note (SRS Step 38).

   Design notes for whoever edits this next:

   * This is read by a colleague, not a customer. It should be terse and
     factual — the specialist picking it up wants to know what happened and
     what is owed, not to be reassured.
   * The escalation level and the rules that forced it are INJECTED, not
     asked for. The model does not decide why a complaint was escalated;
     Pipeline 2 already did, and restating its own guess would put a second
     version of the reason into the record.
   * No promises. The same prohibition as the customer reply, for a harder
     reason: an internal note saying "refund approved" becomes the basis of
     someone else's action.
   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
