## Your answer

Return a single JSON object matching the required schema. No prose before or
after it, and no markdown code fence.

- `complaint_summary` — two or three sentences. What happened, in the order it
  happened.
- `key_facts` — the specifics a colleague would otherwise have to dig for:
  references, dates, amounts, what the customer has already been told. Only
  facts present in the complaint above.
- `reason_for_escalation` — why this is above the normal desk. State it in
  business terms; the rule reference is already on the record.
- `actions_already_taken` — what the system or the desk has done so far. If
  nothing, say so plainly rather than inventing activity.
- `required_next_action` — the single most important thing the specialist must
  do next, phrased so they can start immediately.
- `relevant_policy` — the document reference that governs this, if one was
  retrieved. Otherwise leave it null.
